From c3457dcea8a4390a130397b34df392f7b2f7018f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:57:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: platform: rockchip: Add RKVENC v1 encoder driver

Add a stateful V4L2 memory-to-memory encoder driver for the Rockchip
RKVENC v1 video encoder, found in the RV1126/RV1109 ("vepu541") and
RK3566/RK3568 ("vepu540") SoCs. The hardware produces H.264 (AVC)
and H.265 (HEVC) bitstreams; this driver exposes them through the
standard V4L2 stateful encoder interface.

The code is split into an engine that depends on plain C types only and
a V4L2 front end:

  * The engine (rkvenc-vepu541*.c and rkvenc-{h264,hevc,nal,gop,ref,rc}.c)
    builds the hardware register image, writes the parameter sets
    (SPS/PPS/VPS), manages the GOP structure (a single short-term
    reference, low-delay IDR+P, POC type 0, no B-frames), the two-slot
    reference ping-pong and the per-frame rate control. Pictures whose
    size does not allow P frames are coded as IDR frames only.

  * The front end (rkvenc.c, rkvenc-v4l2.c) binds the engine to the V4L2
    mem2mem framework: format negotiation with SPS/VPS cropping for
    sizes that are not a multiple of the coding block, the control set
    (H.264 profile, level, CABAC or CAVLC, 8x8 transform and loop filter
    controls, the HEVC counterparts, CBR bitrate, GOP size, force
    keyframe), buffer queueing, the device_run to hardware job mapping
    and the hard-IRQ/threaded-IRQ completion model with claim-under-lock
    job ownership and a watchdog. A failed job is cleared with a force
    clear and resets the block only when that does not stop it.

Both V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_HEADER_MODE_SEPARATE and JOINED_WITH_1ST_FRAME
(with PREPEND_SPSPPS_TO_IDR) are supported. Hardware row-level rate
control is left disabled; the driver varies the per-picture QP only.
The raw frames are imported without a kernel mapping and a capture
buffer holds half as many bytes as the picture has pixels, so that 4K
streams fit the vmalloc area of 32-bit systems.

The RK3568 HEVC tiles wider than 1920 pixels and the Q6 VEPU variant
are out of scope.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
